  "id": "mere-exposure-effect",
  "term": "mere-exposure effect",
  "definition": "The mere-exposure effect is the tendency for repeated contact with something that was initially unfamiliar to increase how positively it is felt or liked. In this source, it is described as an affective preference linked to familiarity, with evidence that higher anxiety is associated with a weaker effect.",
